Other files which are needed for this example are the same as in the
"Eirene_bench_difft_physics" run: eirene*.out, geometry_*.inp, 
ue_rect_slab.geom, uedata_rect_slab.u. Note that ratecalc must be used to
generate the netCDF files for hchexold and hionizeir. In hchexold.nc, the
value of sgvmax is left at its default value of 0.0 to effectively disable
rejection, as is done in the EIRENE run. Before compiling
readgeometry and readbackground, the flag UEDGE_RECT_SLAB must be changed
from "0" to "1". A reduced set of tallies, obtained by changing the
flag OPTIMIZE from "0" to "1" in tallysetup, is used for these output
data. 80000 flights were run.